# basename(1)

## NAME

basename - strip directory and suffix from a path

## SYNOPSIS

    basename path [suffix]
    basename -a [-s suffix] path...

## DESCRIPTION

Writes the last component of each path, without trailing slashes. If a suffix such as `.txt` is given and the name ends with it (and is not equal to it), the suffix is removed.

## OPTIONS

- `-a`: accept several paths
- `-s suffix`: remove this suffix (implies `-a`)

## EXAMPLES

    basename /home/note.txt .txt

